---
import {
  Badge,
  Box,
  Button,
  Card,
  Grid,
  GridItem,
  Group,
  Image,
  Section,
  Text,
  Title,
} from "@nautui/core";
---

<Section border={{ top: "md" }}>
  <Title>Card</Title>
  <Box mb="md" border="md">
    <Grid columns={3} border="md">
      <GridItem>
        <Card>
          <Badge variant="flat" iconOnly>
            <svg
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              width="48"
              height="48"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="1.5"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
            >
              <title>Weather</title>
              <path d="M12 2v2" />
              <path d="m4.93 4.93 1.41 1.41" />
              <path d="M20 12h2" />
              <path d="m19.07 4.93-1.41 1.41" />
              <path d="M15.947 12.65a4 4 0 0 0-5.925-4.128" />
              <path d="M13 22H7a5 5 0 1 1 4.9-6H13a3 3 0 0 1 0 6Z" />
            </svg>
          </Badge>
          <Title level={3} mt="md">Continuous Observation</Title>
          <Text>
            Mermind connects to your store and surrounding tools and monitors
            your operations without requiring manual checks or dashboard
            reviews. It works in the background, continuously, so you don't have
            to.
          </Text>

          <Group justify="end">
            <Button href="/about" variant="ghost">
              <span>Learn More</span>
              <svg
                xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                width="20"
                height="20"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.5"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                class="lucide lucide-arrow-right-icon lucide-arrow-right"
              >
                <title>Arrow Right</title>
                <path d="M5 12h14" />
                <path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7" />
              </svg>
            </Button>
          </Group>
        </Card>
      </GridItem>
      <GridItem>
        <Card>
          <Badge variant="flat" iconOnly>
            <svg
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              width="48"
              height="48"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="1.5"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              class="lucide lucide-haze-icon lucide-haze"
            >
              <title>Haze</title>
              <path d="m5.2 6.2 1.4 1.4" />
              <path d="M2 13h2" />
              <path d="M20 13h2" />
              <path d="m17.4 7.6 1.4-1.4" />
              <path d="M22 17H2" />
              <path d="M22 21H2" />
              <path d="M16 13a4 4 0 0 0-8 0" />
              <path d="M12 5V2.5" />
            </svg>
          </Badge>
          <Title level={3} mt="md">Pattern Understanding</Title>
          <Text>
            Over time, Mermind learns what normal looks like for your specific
            store — your products, your workflows, your integrations. When
            something deviates from that baseline, it knows — even when no
            threshold has been crossed.
          </Text>
        </Card>
      </GridItem>
      <GridItem>
        <Card>
          <Badge variant="flat" iconOnly>
            <svg
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              width="48"
              height="48"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="1.5"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              class="lucide lucide-crown-icon lucide-crown"
            >
              <title>Crown</title>
              <path
                d="M11.562 3.266a.5.5 0 0 1 .876 0L15.39 8.87a1 1 0 0 0 1.516.294L21.183 5.5a.5.5 0 0 1 .798.519l-2.834 10.246a1 1 0 0 1-.956.734H5.81a1 1 0 0 1-.957-.734L2.02 6.02a.5.5 0 0 1 .798-.519l4.276 3.664a1 1 0 0 0 1.516-.294z"
              />
              <path d="M5 21h14" />
            </svg>
          </Badge>
          <Title level={3} mt="md">Pattern Understanding</Title>
          <Text>
            Over time, Mermind learns what normal looks like for your specific
            store — your products, your workflows, your integrations. When
            something deviates from that baseline, it knows — even when no
            threshold has been crossed.
          </Text>
        </Card>
      </GridItem>
    </Grid>
  </Box>
  <Box border="md">
    <Grid columns={3}>
      <GridItem>
        <Card shadow="sm" radius="sm" border="md">
          <slot slot="header">
            <Image
              fluid
              src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mantinedev/mantine/master/.demo/images/bg-8.png"
              alt="Example"
            />
          </slot>
          <Title level={3}>Card with Small Border, Radius, and Shadow</Title>
          <Text>
            Over time, Mermind learns what normal looks like for your specific
            store — your products, your workflows, your integrations. When
            something deviates from that baseline, it knows — even when no
            threshold has been crossed.
          </Text>
        </Card>
      </GridItem>
      <GridItem>
        <Card shadow="md" radius="md" border="md">
          <slot slot="header">
            <Image
              fluid
              src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mantinedev/mantine/master/.demo/images/bg-8.png"
              alt="Example"
            />
          </slot>
          <Title level={3}>Card with Medium Border, Radius, and Shadow</Title>
          <Text>
            Over time, Mermind learns what normal looks like for your specific
            store — your products, your workflows, your integrations. When
            something deviates from that baseline, it knows — even when no
            threshold has been crossed.
          </Text>
        </Card>
      </GridItem>
      <GridItem>
        <Card shadow="lg" radius="lg" border="md">
          <slot slot="header">
            <Image
              fluid
              src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mantinedev/mantine/master/.demo/images/bg-8.png"
              alt="Example"
            />
          </slot>
          <Title level={3}>Card with Large Shadow and Radius</Title>
          <Text>
            Over time, Mermind learns what normal looks like for your specific
            store — your products, your workflows, your integrations. When
            something deviates from that baseline, it knows — even when no
            threshold has been crossed.
          </Text>
        </Card>
      </GridItem>
      <GridItem>
        <Card variant="rainbow">
          <Title mt="0" level={3}>Card with Rainbow Variant</Title>
          <Text>
            Over time, Mermind learns what normal looks like for your specific
            store — your products, your workflows, your integrations. When
            something deviates from that baseline, it knows — even when no
            threshold has been crossed.
          </Text>
        </Card>
      </GridItem>
      <GridItem>
        <Card variant="light">
          <Title mt="0" level={3}>Card with Light Variant</Title>
          <Text>
            Over time, Mermind learns what normal looks like for your specific
            store — your products, your workflows, your integrations. When
            something deviates from that baseline, it knows — even when no
            threshold has been crossed.
          </Text>
        </Card>
      </GridItem>
      <GridItem>
        <Card variant="surface" hover="light">
          <Title mt="0" level={3}>Card with Surface Variant</Title>
          <Text>
            Over time, Mermind learns what normal looks like for your specific
            store — your products, your workflows, your integrations. When
            something deviates from that baseline, it knows — even when no
            threshold has been crossed.
          </Text>
        </Card>
      </GridItem>
      <GridItem>
        <Card variant="surface" hover="light" badged>
          <Badge slot="badge" variant="solid">Most Popular</Badge>
          <Title mt="0" level={3}>Card with Badge</Title>
          <Text>
            Over time, Mermind learns what normal looks like for your specific
            store — your products, your workflows, your integrations. When
            something deviates from that baseline, it knows — even when no
            threshold has been crossed.
          </Text>
        </Card>
      </GridItem>
    </Grid>
  </Box>
</Section>
